      },
      "call_made": "The three label columns are turned into a hierarchy: each left-hand Sample Collection label (Peripheral Blood, Archival ..., Baseline or on treatment tumor biopsy core ...) becomes a mark-free level-0 grouping row, each 'Core n' a level-1 row, and the Biomarker Analysis text the activity that carries the marks (level 1, or level 2 under a Core). row_position is renumbered in reading order (header 1-3, body 4-19), so it is not the physical row. Notes-column cells bind to the mark-carrying analysis row.",
      "alternative": "Keep one activity per physical row (10 body rows) named by the Biomarker Analysis text only, carrying the Sample Collection and Core labels in cell_text or joined into the name (e.g. 'Core 1 CD38 and PD-L1 ...').",
      "report_section": "3.3"
    },
    {
      "id": "D12",
      "severity": "medium",
      "location": {
        "page": 24
      },
      "call_made": "Table typed subsidiary: a finer per-cycle breakdown of the single main-SoA row 'Tumor Biopsy, Archival Tumor Tissue Collection, Biomarker Blood Draw - See Biomarker Flow Chart'.",
      "alternative": "Type it main_soa as an independent schedule with its own column set (its columns are not a strict refinement of the main SoA's columns: it adds Cycle 2, Cycle 3 and 'Cycle 5 and Beyond' and drops D8/D15).",
      "report_section": "3.1"
    },
